From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: ufs-qcom: do not enable the lane clocks twice

ufs_qcom_disable_lane_clks() is guarded by host->is_lane_clks_enabled
but ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() is not. Since commit c1553fc105df
("scsi: ufs: ufs-qcom: Disable lane clocks during phy hibern8") the
enable runs from ufs_qcom_setup_clocks() PRE_CHANGE whenever the link is
in hibern8, and ufs_qcom_resume() enables the same clocks again a moment
later. The disable only runs once, so every runtime resume leaks one
prepare/enable reference on every clock in the bulk list, which on
SM8550/SM8750 is the whole set: AHB, AXI, aggre AXI, UniPro core, ICE
and the lane symbol clocks.

On the AYN Odin 3 the counts reach several hundred within an hour of
uptime. At system suspend the single disable cannot bring them to zero,
so the UFS clocks stay prepared through suspend-to-idle, GPLL0 and GPLL4
stay requested, and with them the XO. The SoC never enters AOSS deep
sleep and the device draws well over 100 mA all night.

Restore the guard the function had before the clk_bulk conversion so a
second enable is a no-op, matching the disable side.

Fixes: c1553fc105df ("scsi: ufs: ufs-qcom: Disable lane clocks during phy hibern8")

--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -356,6 +356,9 @@
 {
 	int err;
 
+	if (host->is_lane_clks_enabled)
+		return 0;
+
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(host->num_clks, host->clks);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
